<p><br />
This email serves as notification of the above passenger request to travel with their Service Dog. Qantas Specific Needs has assessed the application and believes the Service dog meets the Criteria for Carriage and therefore the criteria for approval.<br />
<br />
<span style="font-size:11pt"><span style="line-height:107%"><span style="font-family:Aptos,sans-serif"><b><u><span style="font-size:10.0pt"><span style="line-height:107%">Service Dogs Conditions of Carriage</span></span></u></b></span></span></span></p>

<ol>
	<li>The passenger has agreed to the Service Dogs Conditions of Carriage. This includes, but is not limited to, the following being adhered to:</li>
	<li>Care for the Service Dog inflight is the responsibility of the passenger.</li>
	<li>The Service Dog must not occupy a seat or sit on the passenger’s lap.</li>
	<li>In economy class, two seats have been allocated, generally one window seat for the Service Dog and the adjacent seat for the passenger.</li>
	<li>The Service Dog must be placed on a moisture absorbent mat on the floor in front of the space allocated to the Service Dog. Airports must provide the moisture absorbent mat.&nbsp; For safety reasons, the Service Dog must be restrained by attaching its leash to the aircraft seat leg, seat track ring or other tether point approved by the operator. The leash should have the ability to be shortened or lengthened as required. For safety reasons, the Service Dog should not be secured directly from its collar or to the aircraft seatbelt being worn by a passenger.&nbsp;</li>
	<li>The passenger and the Service Dog must not be seated in an exit row.</li>
	<li>The Pilot in Command has the final decision as to whether or not the Service Dog is carried on the day of travel and may impose any further conditions that he or she requires in the interests of safety.</li>
	<li>Qantas reserves the right to take any action necessary to ensure the safety of the aircraft, including in circumstances where the Service Dog is behaving in an uncontrollable, aggressive, and/or dangerous manner.</li>
	<li><span style="color:#e74c3c;"><strong>For international travel</strong></span> - the passenger must ensure that the correct documentation (including inoculation certificates or entry permits) is carried with them in their carry-on baggage at all times to ensure that the Service Dog can lawfully depart the country of origin and be cleared for entry into the country of arrival. Under no circumstances will Qantas accept liability for the failure of entry clearance of the Service Dog at the destination or any other arrival port, including due to incorrect or insufficient documentation.</li>
</ol>

<p>Should you require any further information, please do not hesitate to contact us on +61 2 9123 7471 – Option 3.</p>
